>> title: Orejas
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: pastry, sugar, mexican, laminated, oven
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: oreja, orejas, orejitas, palmier, palmiers, elephant ears, palmeras
>> pairs-with: hojaldre, campechanas
>> servings: 24
>> time: 1 hr 10 min
>> step.1: roll out on sugar, not flour
>> step.2: brush, roll both edges in, chill 30 min
>> step.3: slice and press the cut faces in sugar
>> step.4: bake at 400°F 12 min, turn at 8

Roll @hojaldre{1%kg}(one batch, cold) to a 10-by-16-inch rectangle on a bench dusted heavily with @granulated sugar{1 1/2%cup}(300 g). Sugar on the bench instead of flour is the whole recipe — it presses into the leaves and caramelises there.

Brush @&(~1)sugared sheet{} with @water{2%tsp}(10 mL), then roll both long edges in to meet at the middle and ~chill{30%min} until firm enough to cut cleanly.

Slice @&(~1)chilled log{} into 1/2-inch pieces and press each cut face into @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g), flattening it a little as you go so the ear opens in the oven.

Bake @&(~1)cut pieces{} at 400°F for ~bake{12%min}, turning each one over at 8 minutes so both faces catch. They come out limp and crisp as they cool; lift them off the tray before the sugar sets them to it.
